From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 23:15:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: wait for display mutex probe before bind

of_find_device_by_node() only guarantees that the display mutex platform
device exists.  Its driver may still be deferred on clocks or power
domains, leaving the device drvdata unset.

Do not continue aggregate bind until the mutex driver has completed probe.
This keeps mtk_crtc_create() from passing a NULL mutex context to
mtk_mutex_get().  Returning -EPROBE_DEFER from the aggregate bind also
rolls back the triggering DSI component attach so it can be retried after
suppliers become available.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
index 0a48aaf..fb88d8f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
@@ -648,6 +648,13 @@ static int mtk_drm_bind(struct device *dev)
 		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 	}
 
+	if (!platform_get_drvdata(pdev)) {
+		dev_dbg(dev, "Waiting for disp-mutex driver %pOF\n",
+			private->mutex_node);
+		put_device(&pdev->dev);
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+	}
+
 	private->mutex_dev = &pdev->dev;
 	private->mtk_drm_bound = true;
 	private->dev = dev;
-- 
